    "body": "MantleOS 2.0.0rc1 is the breaking reference-platform consolidation release.\n\nHighlights:\n\n- one canonical evidence-grounded resident runtime and Body command dispatcher\n- `mantle-resident-v2`, `mantle-germ-v2`, host evidence v3, and GUI nerve coverage v3\n- target-bound hatch/graft authorization with transactional staging, resume, quarantine, inert migration, and preserved rebind\n- C/C++/Qt/CMake and Rust fallback coverage with explicit `COMPLETE`, `PARTIAL`, and `BLOCKED` results\n- Action Execution Proofs, metabolic ceilings/receipts, bounded resource offers, face attestations, lineage labels, and read-only ancestry\n- maintained NotepadNext Mantle 2 candidate and Organize.AppAI migration\n- Windows, Python 3.10\u20133.14, mutation, Hermes, browser, and package/release CI\n\nBreaking migration requirements:\n\n- legacy germs and residents remain inspectable but require explicit `migrate-*` commands\n- maintained residents must declare `mantle-resident-v2`\n- external hatch/graft activation requires one fresh artifact-and-target-bound operator authorization\n\nVerification for commit `c98a3031f830735f6b64fd9c6792b882fcbf00d5`:\n\n- Python 3.10\u20133.14 certification: PASS\n- Windows strict certification: PASS\n- targeted mutation sweep: PASS\n- Hermes integration/adversarial containment: PASS\n- browser examples: PASS\n- wheel/sdist build, metadata validation, clean install, CLI smoke, hash/private-path scan: PASS\n\nThe attached manifest hashes the distributions and exact CI/application/example receipts. It is evidence only and grants no resident runtime authority.\n\nKnown boundary: Mantle's Python runner is bounded but is not a hard WASM sandbox. Hostile operators, malicious in-process Body code, arbitrary tool-calling MINDs, multi-agent coordination, and real OS credential adapters remain outside this release.\n\nPyPI publication is intentionally not part of this prerelease.\n"
