    "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jodydugas-ctrl/mantle-os/tarball/v1.3.0",
    "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jodydugas-ctrl/mantle-os/zipball/v1.3.0",
    "body": "## Mantle OS 1.3.0\n\nThis release completes the release-hardening and Hermes resident-addon work while keeping production MIND fusion dormant and fail-closed until separately authenticated operator and guardian approvals exist.\n\n### Highlights\n\n- Reversible, receipt-backed MIND fusion and authority-free defusion.\n- One fixed 600-second natural cognitive scheduler per fused resident, with a bounded queue for additional nociceptive wakeups.\n- Hermes-native cognition through the host-owned `PluginContext.llm` provider/model abstraction.\n- Rolling token/cost budgets, one addon dispatch through host-owned fallback/retries, request timeouts, outage handling, serialized cognition, conservative unknown-usage charging, and redacted usage receipts.\n- Distinct Ed25519-authenticated, target-bound operator and guardian approval verification using verifier-only public keys.\n- Symlink-safe, owner-only atomic persistence.\n- A complete tracked 146-file Mantle OS snapshot in the Hermes addon example.\n- Canonical runtime/security certification focused on 90 executable behavior contracts; mutable optimization inventories and version snapshots remain advisory release checks.\n\n### Certification\n\n- `python -m mantle check`: 14 passed, 0 skipped, 0 failed.\n- Security invariants: 90/90.\n- Hermes addon: 127 tests passed with `ResourceWarning` treated as errors.\n- Vendor parity: 146/146 tracked files aligned.\n- Repository alignment: 348 files, no failures.\n- Adversarial containment: 11/11.\n- Installed-wheel proof: 90/90.\n\n### Release artifacts\n\n- Commit: `cf1796d03b6acebbbb6255566aadf48d96ca61a8`\n- Wheel: `mantle_os-1.3.0-py3-none-any.whl`\n- Wheel SHA-256: `b8a49f03716436593ccc16c5438a6d2d33166e0f5995271757ef67ad2af6f7c1`\n\n### Production authority state\n\nPublication does **not** activate production cognition. Operator and guardian decisions remain deferred, production fusion remains disabled, and reproduction remains disabled. The authenticated lifecycle was exercised with deterministic test-only authority and a controlled host-model fixture; those fixtures are not production approval.\n\nSee [`CHANGELOG.md`](https://github.com/jodydugas-ctrl/mantle-os/blob/v1.3.0/CHANGELOG.md) for the complete change list and [`SECURITY.md`](https://github.com/jodydugas-ctrl/mantle-os/blob/v1.3.0/SECURITY.md) for reporting guidance.\n"
  },
